  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 135 AM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nThe forecast this week is going to be a rinse and repeat each day as \nthe center of the ridge of high pressure sits near the Four Corners \nregion. Daily afternoon highs max out in the mid-to-upper 90s for \nmost, except for lower triple digits along the Pecos River and Rio \nGrande Valleys. Long-range model guidance suggests the possibility \nof convection in portions of west Texas and southeast New Mexico \nnext weekend as shortwave impulses round the eastern periphery of \nthe ridge. However, there is a lot of uncertainty in the details at \nthis time.  \n  \nGreening",
